      "id": "001",
      "headline": "Sir Reginald Snorewell Declares Napping a Professional Sport, Demands Olympic Medal",
      "summary": "The self-proclaimed 'horizontal champion' has submitted a 400-page petition to the International Olympic Committee.",
      "fullBody": "Sir Reginald Snorewell, a professional napper from Snorington-on-Sea, has filed a formal petition to have napping recognized as an Olympic sport. 'I've been training for 47 years,' Snorewell said from his recliner. 'My 3-hour afternoon naps have perfect form.' Opponents argue that snoring is not athleticism, but Snorewell counters, 'Tell that to my gold medal in REM cycling.'",
      "category": "sports",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-06-09/001.jpg",
      "publishedAt": "3 hrs ago",
      "readTimeSeconds": 62,
      "tags": ["Sports", "Satire", "Napping"],
      "isBreaking": false
    },
    {
      "id": "002",
      "headline": "Bing Bong Wobblebottom Sues Own Shadow for 'Constant Stalking and Mimicry'",
      "summary": "The lawsuit demands $2 million or 'a less embarrassing silhouette.'",
      "fullBody": "Bing Bong Wobblebottom, a part-time clown from Wobbletown, has filed a restraining order against his own shadow, claiming it has been 'imitating his every move for decades.' 'I can't even wave without it waving back,' Wobblebottom complained. The judge dismissed the case, ruling that shadows are 'legally incapable of malicious intent.' Wobblebottom plans to appeal, saying, 'That's exactly what my shadow would want me to think.'",
      "category": "weird",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-06-09/002.jpg",
      "publishedAt": "5 hrs ago",
