    {
      "id": "046",
      "headline": "Sir Snoozealot McPillow Declares Alarm Clocks 'Instruments Of Oppression'",
      "summary": "He has started a movement called 'The Resistance Rests.'",
      "fullBody": "Sir Snoozealot McPillow has declared war on alarm clocks, calling them 'tyrannical noisemakers' and 'dream interrupters.' 'Sleep is a right, not a suggestion,' McPillow announced from his bed. His movement, 'The Resistance Rests,' encourages followers to 'snooze with purpose.' Members wear pajamas as protest attire and communicate only in yawns. McPillow's manifesto, written on a pillowcase, concludes: 'We will sleep in, and they will hear us snore.'",
      "category": "weird",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-06-09/046.jpg",
      "publishedAt": "3 days ago",
      "readTimeSeconds": 66,
      "tags": ["Weird", "Satire", "Sleep"],
      "isBreaking": false
    },
    {
      "id": "047",
      "headline": "Professor Wobble McMumble Discovers That Naps Are 'Time Travel To Snack O'Clock'",
      "summary": "The study found that 20-minute naps somehow consume three hours of your day.",
      "fullBody": "Professor Wobble McMumble has published a study claiming that naps are actually a form of time travel that transports you directly to 'snack o'clock.' 'You close your eyes at 2 PM, and suddenly it's 5 PM and you're hungry,' McMumble explained. 'That's temporal physics.' The study also found that naps create a 'snack debt' that must be repaid with interest. McMumble's next research will investigate why 'quick naps' last longer than 'full sleeps.'",
      "category": "science",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-06-09/047.jpg",
      "publishedAt": "5 days ago",
      "readTimeSeconds": 68,
      "tags": ["Science", "Satire", "Sleep"],
      "isBreaking": false
    },
    {
      "id": "048",
      "headline": "Senator Bluster McPuff Declares Silence 'Golden' Then Won't Stop Talking About It",
      "summary": "His speech on the virtue of silence lasted 4 hours and 27 minutes.",
      "fullBody": "Senator Bluster McPuff delivered a 4-hour speech declaring silence 'golden' and 'underrated.' 'We should all appreciate the beauty of quiet contemplation,' McPuff said loudly, before continuing for another 3 hours. Observers noted the irony. 'He's been talking about silence for longer than most movies,' one staffer whispered. McPuff concluded by recommending everyone 'think about being quiet' before immediately scheduling another press conference on the same topic.",
      "category": "politics",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-06-09/048.jpg",
